  "final_text": "All four steps are done.\n\n1. **Data view:** \"Kibana Sample Data Logs\" covers the index `kibana_sample_data_logs`. Its time field is `timestamp`.\n2. **Dashboard:** \"S4-7170ecc7 Web logs\" has two panels. \"Requests over time\" is a line chart of request counts by `timestamp`. \"Requests by response code\" is a bar chart of counts by `response.keyword`.\n3. **Alert rule:** \"S4-7170ecc7 5xx errors\" is an Elasticsearch query rule that checks every minute. It fires when more than 10 requests with a response code from 500 to 599 arrive within 5 minutes. It matches `response.keyword` between \"500\" and \"599\". That comparison is alphabetical, which works because all codes have three digits. The rule was created disabled, so I enabled it.\n4. **Panel edit:** The second panel is now titled \"Responses by code\". Reading the rule back shows it enabled, with status ok.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
